@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-4 py-md-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-9">
            <div class="mb-4">
                <h1 class="display-6 fw-semibold">Privacy Policy</h1>
                <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                    How Adopt-A-Pet handles your information.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
                    <p>
                        Adopt-A-Pet helps people publish pets available
                        for adoption and connect with potential adopters.
                        This page explains what information the application
                        stores and how it is used.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">1. Information We Collect</h2>
                    <p>When you use the application, we may store:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Account information:</strong>
                            your email address and authentication-related
                            information required to manage your account.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Pet listings:</strong>
                            information you submit about a pet, such as
                            its name, species, breed, age, description,
                            location and optional image URL.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Adoption requests:</strong>
                            the message you submit, the request status
                            and information linking the request to your
                            account and the relevant pet.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">2. How Information Is Used</h2>
                    <p>
                        Information is used to operate the application,
                        display available pets, manage listings, process
                        adoption requests and enforce access permissions.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">3. Information Visibility</h2>
                    <p>
                        Pet listing information is displayed to visitors
                        so they can discover pets available for adoption.
                        Adoption request messages and management details
                        are intended for the applicant and the owner of
                        the relevant pet, subject to the application's
                        access controls.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Avoid including passwords, financial details or
                        other sensitive personal information in pet
                        descriptions or adoption messages.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">4. Data Storage and Retention</h2>
                    <p>
                        Application data is stored on our side.
                        Account and listing information may remain stored
                        while the relevant records exist. Deleting a pet
                        listing may also delete its associated adoption
                        request records.
                    </p>

                   

    
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-4">
                <a asp-controller="Home"
                   asp-action="Index"
                   class="btn btn-outline-success">
                    Back to Home
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
